{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1513366090,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyODI1MjQ0MTM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2032","origin":"github"},"title":"What should search do different by default?","message":"@yarikoptic We had quite a few discussions on what to do differently. Given that the `///` is not a viable beast to play with, I decided to take a few datasets from it, reaggregate them and re-published them (without data). I will use this to implement further tests. Moreover, I would be glad to get comments on the default behavior. I give a sample below. Please chime in with your feedback and suggestions.\n\nThe following protocol is what is possible after a plain reaggregation, without any change in the dataset configuration.\n\n```sh\n% datalad install -s http://psydata.ovgu.de/aggdemo/demo/ aggdemo\n[INFO   ] Cloning http://psydata.ovgu.de/aggdemo/demo/ to '/tmp/aggdemo' \n[INFO   ] access to dataset sibling \"psydata\" not auto-enabled, enable with:\n|               datalad siblings -d \"/tmp/aggdemo\" enable -s psydata \ninstall(ok): /tmp/aggdemo (dataset)\n% cd aggdemo\n% datalad search\n[INFO   ] Building search index \n[INFO   ] Scanning for metadata keys \n[INFO   ] Added 1 document on dataset . \n[INFO   ] Added 9457 documents on dataset crcns-vim-2 \n[INFO   ] Added 4 documents on dataset openfmri \n[INFO   ] Added 134 documents on dataset openfmri/ds000001 \n[INFO   ] Added 280 documents on dataset openfmri/ds000002 \n[INFO   ] Search index contains 9876 documents \n% datalad search nishimoto\n[INFO   ] Query completed in 0.00141906738281 sec. Reporting up to 20 top matches. \nsearch(ok): crcns-vim-2\n% datalad search poldrack\n[INFO   ] Query completed in 0.00161004066467 sec. Reporting up to 20 top matches. \nsearch(ok): openfmri/ds000002\nsearch(ok): openfmri/ds000001\nsearch(ok): openfmri\naction summary:\n  search (ok: 3)\n% datalad search POldr